   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**The biggest gaps are in sub-Saharan Africa.** Among countries reporting recent data, primary schools without electricity account for:\n\n- **99% in Chad** (2024)\n- **92% in Niger** (2024)\n- **90% in DR Congo** (2023)\n- **88% in Madagascar** (2024)\n- **83% in Sierra Leone** (2024)\n\nThe map shows each country’s latest reported value from **2020–2025**, covering 153 countries and territories. Countries without recent data are missing—not necessarily fully electrified.\n\nSource: UIS, February 2026 release.",
